rloo Underground Station","to":"12A MEPHAM STREET, LONDON","towards":null}],"reason":null,"name":"London Waterloo"}],"bestHub":{"name":"Leicester Square","minutes":58},"missing":[]},"summary":"<p><strong>Stylish 2-Bedroom Ground Floor Apartment – Osterley, TW7</strong></p><div><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">A beautifully presented two-bedroom ground floor apartment set within the charming Art Deco-style Osterley Court, ideally located on the Great West Road in the heart of Osterley. This well-maintained home offers a blend of period character and modern finishes, just a short walk from Osterley Tube Station and the open green spaces of Osterley Park.</span></p></div><p><strong>Property Description</strong></p><div><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">This well-presented ground floor apartment offers a stylish and comfortable living space within a charming Art Deco mansion block. The property features a modern kitchen arranged along three walls, complete with sleek quartz worktops and integrated appliances, ideal for both everyday use and entertaining. The lounge and hallway are finished with wooden flooring, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere. Two generously sized bedrooms provide ample accommodation, while the fully tiled contemporary bathroom adds a touch of luxury with its modern fittings. Residents also benefit from secure entry, access to landscaped communal gardens, and on-site parking (subject to availability).</span></p></div><p><strong>Transport Links</strong></p><div><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Perfectly positioned for commuters, the apartment is just a 2-minute walk from Osterley Tube Station on the Piccadilly Line, offering direct services to Heathrow Terminals 1–5 in under 20 minutes and Central London in around 30 minutes. Syon Lane Station is also nearby, providing South Western Railway connections to London Waterloo. A range of local bus routes—including the H91, H28, and 120—ensure convenient travel across West London, linking the property to Hounslow, Ealing, Brentford, and Southall with ease.</span></p></div><p><strong>Local Amenities</strong></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Shops & Dining</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Osterley Court is close to Hounslow and Brentford town centre, both offering supermarkets, high street shops, and essential services. For a more relaxed vibe, Osterley Village features independent cafés, family-run restaurants, and local stores.</span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Green Spaces & Leisure</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Enjoy the scenic grounds of Osterley Park and House just a short walk away. The area also offers access to Thistleworth Tennis Club, Indian Gymkhana, Wycombe House Cricket Club, and Wyke Green Golf Club—ideal for sports and leisure.</span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Schools and Education</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Families benefit from proximity to respected schools including Nishkam School West London, The Green School for Girls, Isleworth & Syon School, and Spring Grove Primary School.</span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Local Pubs & Dining Spots</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Popular local venues include The Hare & Hounds for classic pub fare, Tiger Lily for Asian cuisine, and Ballucci Isleworth for artisan coffee and light bites.</span></p><p><strong><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Major Employers</span></strong></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">The property is ideally located near major employers such as Sky Group HQ, West Middlesex University Hospital, and Heathrow Airport, making it a great choice for professionals working in media, healthcare, or aviation.</span></p><p><strong>📌 Additional Information</strong></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0cm\"><li><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Unfurnished</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">EPC Rating: C</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Council Tax: Band D – £2,185.56 per annum (London Borough of Hounslow)</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Deposit: £2,192</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Rent: £1900</span></li><li><span style=\"font-family:'palatino linotype' , serif\">Available from: 9th Nov 2026</span></li></ul>","keyFeatures":["2-Bed Ground Floor Flat","Modern Kitchen with integrated appliances.","Wood floors &amp; tiled bathroom.","Top Transport Links, 2 mins to Osterley Station (Piccadilly Line).","Shops Nearby Close to Hounslow, Brentford &amp; Osterley Village.","Green &amp; Active Near Osterley Park, tennis &amp; golf clubs.","Good Schools Near Nishkam, Green School &amp; Spring Grove.","Local Dining Hare &amp; Hounds, Tiger Lily, Ballucci.","Work Hubs, Nearby Close to Sky HQ, West Mid Hospital &amp; Heathrow.","Secure &amp; Peaceful Living, Gated entry, communal gardens &amp; resident parking."],"outcode":"TW7","images":[{"url":"https://media.rightmove.co.uk/property-photo/1cba3269d/95227263/1cba3269d8558e96a0100cc6085cded5.jpeg","kind":"photo","caption":null},{"url":"https://media.rightmove.co.uk/property-photo/460224e89/95227263/460224e896a8724a4ded4cc0ccc5affa.jpeg","kind":"photo","caption":null},{"url":"https://media.rightmove.co.uk/property-photo/1370cbdd1/95227263/1370cbdd1d4506cde2bff089ad2d7144.jpeg","kind":"photo","caption":null},{"url":"https://media.rightmove.co.uk/property-photo/3dd00bfa5/95227263/3dd00bfa5f0486178c2151ef8d079f8a.jpeg","kind":"photo","caption":null},{"url":"https://media.rightmove.co.uk/prope